# VibeOS Settings' "Set PIN" and "Set pattern" (vibeos-set-own-password, run as root through pkexec): the current PIN,
# pattern or password checked as the lock screen checks it (/etc/pam.d/vibeos), then the new one written by pam_unix
# alone. As root pam_unix asks for no old password and applies no length or similarity rule, which a four-digit PIN
# would fail; the login keyring is moved to the new password by Settings itself (vibeos-keyring-rekey).
@include common-auth
@include common-account
password	required	pam_unix.so yescrypt
